{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6KwVGNJW1khGLU2YZwjJU","type":"tool_result","content":"2144 PLAN.md\n1:# Eye of the Bolt-Holder\n11:## 0. Ground rules for the builders\n27:## 1. Research summary\n29:### 1.1 The source, and what we keep\n58:### 1.2 The engine (my-3D2dge v0.85.2)\n91:### 1.3 AI Hub (Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n112:## 2. The game at a glance\n143:## 3. Architecture\n145:### 3.1 Stack (pinned)\n159:### 3.2 Fetching (tested during planning; about 12 MB)\n174:### 3.3 Folder layout\n233:### 3.4 The build: one HTML file\n267:### 3.5 Runtime layers\n298:### 3.6 State (also the save format; version 1)\n320:### 3.7 Scenes and flow\n341:### 3.8 Units and conventions\n349:### 3.9 Engine changes to make (log them in PATCHES.md)\n363:## 4. Systems and mechanics\n367:### 4.1 Movement and the grid\n384:### 4.2 Dungeon features and the wiring language\n445:### 4.3 The party: races, classes, stats, formation\n476:### 4.4 Character creation (`create` scene)\n495:### 4.5 Items, inventory, equipment and the Hand\n520:### 4.6 Combat (real time)\n574:### 4.7 Monsters and their AI\n576:#### 4.7.1 Size and cells\n581:#### 4.7.2 Minds (per type in §7.6)\n597:#### 4.7.3 Attacks\n602:#### 4.7.4 The Bolt-Holder (boss, floor 4)\n620:### 4.8 Magic\n647:### 4.9 Camp, rest and food\n662:### 4.10 Experience, levels and hidden deeds\n670:### 4.11 Down, death, raising and game over\n677:### 4.12 NPCs, dialogue and choices\n689:### 4.13 Messages, Examine, Journal, notes and hints\n703:### 4.14 Automap\n712:### 4.15 Saves\n720:### 4.16 Settings (the engine's, plus a *Game* group)\n737:## 5. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller-first\n739:### 5.1 Principles\n753:### 5.2 The play HUD (over the full-screen 3D view)\n772:### 5.3 Screens\n813:### 5.4 Focus navigation and the mouse\n828:### 5.5 Prompts and glyphs\n842:### 5.6 Input map (all rebindable except the menu actions)\n872:### 5.7 Touch-only devices\n881:## 6. Presentation: art, animation and audio\n883:### 6.1 Art direction\n908:### 6.2 The 3D presenter (`40–44`)\n949:### 6.3 Creature recipes\n982:### 6.4 Animation list (new, on the engine's rigs, tweens and pen)\n989:### 6.5 Audio: code only, no files\n1048:## 7. Content\n1050:### 7.1 World bible (all original)\n1062:### 7.2 Writing style guide\n1097:### 7.3 Story beats and cutscenes\n1139:### 7.4 The floors\n1169:#### 7.4.1 Floor 1: The Hasp Drains (22×17)\n1286:#### 7.4.2 Floor 2: The Tumbler Halls (22×17)\n1410:#### 7.4.3 Floor 3: The Gloam Deeps (24×18)\n1515:#### 7.4.4 Floor 4: The Eye's Vault (13×14)\n1572:### 7.5 The Rat Run (race floor, 14×12; hub ghost race and solo time trial)\n1606:### 7.6 Bestiary\n1637:### 7.7 Items\n1726:### 7.8 Spells\n1751:### 7.9 The party, the NPCs and their scripts\n1818:## 8. Dev Mode (from the pause menu; hidden in hub sessions)\n1840:## 9. Attract mode\n1872:## 10. Multiplayer\n1874:### 10.1 AI Hub session (`AIHub.active`): the Rat Run ghost race, 1 to 4 players\n1905:### 10.2 On its own\n1914:## 11. About and Credits, and the final report\n1959:## 12. Build order and milestones\n1976:## 13. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1996:## 14. Testing\n1998:### 14.1 The one command\n2006:### 14.2 The Node harness (as in `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`)\n2032:### 14.3 Suites and what they check\n2056:### 14.4 The scripted full playthrough\n2076:### 14.5 Browser checks\n2095:### 14.6 Looking (only what scripts can't judge)\n2124:## 15. Definition of done (TASK.md coverage)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d562a4a4-1880-473a-a05f-38e08e0d0050","uuid":"889e74e5-ad2c-4e8a-937f-eb60c768752b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:50:56.474Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2144 PLAN.md\n1:# Eye of the Bolt-Holder\n11:## 0. Ground rules for the builders\n27:## 1. Research summary\n29:### 1.1 The source, and what we keep\n58:### 1.2 The engine (my-3D2dge v0.85.2)\n91:### 1.3 AI Hub (Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n112:## 2. The game at a glance\n143:## 3. Ar