{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xiho6Zp6PemJ19eQazi2zN","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (331.5KB). Full output saved to: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261103-185046--x53986f-work/d562a4a4-1880-473a-a05f-38e08e0d0050/tool-results/bhds9ajgr.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n1: <!DOCTYPE html>\n2: <!--\n3:   my-3D2dge (My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine), 3D crawler kit v0.85.2 (dev-build)\n4:   https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n5: \n6:   AI MODELS: this one file is the engine, the 3D engine, their documentation and one 3D game to copy.\n7:     1. Read the 3D engine's manual: the comment at the top of the script marked \"inlined from engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js\".\n8:        Then the API card in <script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\"> below, for what the 2D engine still does in\n9:        a 3D game: the game and its scenes, input, the rigs and their moves, the HUD (font, ui, menus), sound.\n10:     2. The engines are the scripts marked \"inlined from engine/...\". They are yours to change: fix, extend or rewrite\n8:       Then the API card in <script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\"> below, for what the 2D engine still does in\n38:<script type=\"text/markdown\" id=\"my3d2dge-api\">\n249:- **Modules** (`engine/modules/<name>.js`; `modules/` in the handoff package): general systems in files of their own, each a `<script>` after the engine, its header its manual (read it there, or its section of the index). A kit carries the modules its slice names (`@modules` in its header); the full engine (`dist/my-3d2dge.js`; `my-3d2dge.js` in the handoff package) carries them all.\n263:</script>\n264:<script type=\"importmap\">\n273:</script>\n274:<style>\n291:<body>\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d562a4a4-1880-473a-a05f-38e08e0d0050","uuid":"e762caff-5a20-4ac1-9f