{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghBfD7yn2DMYVTsB2GLz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ey3hnj4XoAdqWAdcyk97nM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine patches\n\nEvery change to the engines, small and marked `PATCH (Eye of the Bolt-Holder)` in the source.\n\n## engine/my-3d2dge.js (the 2D engine, v0.85.2)\n\n1. **Beards and shut eyes** (`E.Humanoid` head drawing). New rig options `beard: 'full' | 'braided'` (drawn in the\n   hair's colour over the jaw, in `draw` and therefore in `drawPortrait`) and `eyesShut: true` (eyes drawn closed, for\n   Sister Veil). Why: the dwarves need beards and Veil keeps her eyes shut; the rig had neither.\n2. **Button symbols** (the standard `glyphs` setting). Defaults to PlayStation and offers only PlayStation and Xbox.\n   Why: the task's controller-first rule (PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox option).\n3. **A voice bus** (`game.audio`). A third gain bus beside sfx and music, with `audio.voiceVolume`, and\n   `audio.bus('sfx' | 'music' | 'voice')` to reach a bus. Why: the babble synth plays on its own bus under its own\n   Voices volume setting.\n4. **Panned sound effects** (`audio.sfx(name, { pan })`). A StereoPannerNode in front of the sfx bus when `pan` is given.\n   Why: flank and rear hits and monster sounds are placed by bearing.\n5. **Options ignored while Create is held** (the pausable scene's pause check). Why: the AI Hub's rule (Create +\n   Options opens the hub's corner bar).\n6. **`saves.canLoad`** (the pause menu's Save/Load hook). `false` hides Load. Why: an AI Hub session has no saves.\n\n## engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js (the 3D engine, v0.85.2)\n\n1. **`world.wallBlock({ x, y, w, d, h, spec })`**: a block made from exactly the level's wall materials (the level keeps\n   its side and top material makers as `L._sideMat` and `L._topMat`). Why: secret walls that sink into the floor and\n   illusory walls must be indistinguishable from the walls around them, and `world.box` uses a different material.\n\nNothing else in either engine was changed. The pause menu's own `items` already accepted a function (checked, not\npatched), so a session's menu hides Dev Mode, Journal and About by returning nothing.\nEOF\ncat > CONTENT.md <<'EOF'\n# Content formats (for designers)\n\nEverything a floor is lives in `src/15-data-floors.js` as data; the game reads it, the tests lint it, the bot walks it.\n\n## A floor\n\n```js\nB.FLOORS.f1 = {\n  name, card,               // the floor's name and its one line on the floor card\n  song, step, over,         // its song (B.SONGS), footstep sound family, the game-over line\n  look: { ground: [base, dark, light], groundStyle: 'tiles' | 'plain' (flagstone by default), water, runes, side, color,\n          fog: [color, near, far], ambient: [sky, ground, power], torch },\n  map: ['#####', ...],      // one character a cell (below)\n  start: [x, y, dir],       // dir 0 N, 1 E, 2 S, 3 W\n  water: [[x0, y0, x1, y1]],// cells with a water channel painted on the floor\n  doors: { id: [x, y, { lock: itemId, lk: 'simple' | 'warded', secret, undergate }] },\n  plates: { id: [x, y, 'hold' | 'latch' | 'toggle'] }, traps: { id: [x, y] },\n  pits: { id: [x, y, { trapdoor }] }, fall: { to, at: [x, y, dir] },\n  tps: { id: [x, y, { to: [x, y, dir], silent, loops: [[n, textId or barkId]] }] },\n  feats: [[id, kind, x, y, face, { text, holds: [itemIds], accepts, look }]],\n  wires: [{ when, mode: 'hold', do: [actions], fail: [actions], once, failAfter }],\n  items: [[x, y, itemId, n]], mons: [[x, y, type, n, { asleep, patrol: [[x, y]], id, sight, half, death, group, fixed }]],\n  npcs: [[id, x, y, dir, { ghost, hidden }]],\n  stairs: { 'x,y': { to, at } | { sealed: textId } | { finish: true } | { to, at, ladder: true } },\n  safe: [[x0, y0, x1, y1]], wander: { budget, groups: [[type, n]], at: [[x, y]] },\n  hints: [{ cells: [[x, y]], after: seconds, text, done: { plateDown | open | flag } }],\n  waypoints: [[name, x, y, dir]], areas: { name: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }, walk: [bot steps]\n};\n```\n\n**Map characters:** `#` wall, `.` floor, `@` start, `<` `>` stairs, `+` door, `=` gate, `L` `K` locked door, `M` magic\nseal, `H` secret wall, `I` illusory wall, `P` plate, `T` dart trap, `O` pit, `o` trapdoor, `^` teleporter, `S` spinner,\n`U` the Undergate, `*` a pit's landing, `B` the boss.\n\n**Wall features** stand on the open cell `(x, y)` and face the wall at `face` (N, E, S, W). Kinds: `lever`, `button`,\n`catch` (look `stone` or `rivet`), `alcove`, `shrine`, `gearNiche`, `clockFace`, `plaque` (text), `candle`,\n`greatLock`, `raiseShrine`, `undergate`, `torch` (a brazier niche), and decor: `grate`, `pipe`, `chain`, `gearWall`,\n`eyeRelief`.\n\n## The wiring language\n\nTriggers (`when`): `{ lever }`, `{ button }`, `{ buttons: [ids] }` (all within the Button window), `{ catch }`,\n`{ plate }`, `{ plates: [ids] }` (all down), `{ alcove, item | kind }`, `{ alcovesFull: [ids] }`, `{ killed: [ids] }`,\n`{ flag }`, `{ sequence: [feature ids] }` (in order; a wrong one runs `fail`), `{ levers: { id: on } }` (a combination;\na wrong set after all have moved runs `fail`), `{ enter: [x, y] }`, `{ enterArea: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }`.\n`mode: 'hold'` runs `do` while the trigger holds and its inverse when it lets go.\n\nActions (`do`, `fail`): `['open' | 'close' | 'toggle', doorId]`, `['bridge', pitId]`, `['pitOpen', pitId]`,\n`['teleporter', id, on]`, `['msg', textId]`, `['hint', textId]`, `['story', nodeId]`, `['bark', barkId]`,\n`['give', itemId, [x, y] | featureId]`, `['spawn', type, [x, y], n]`, `['xp', n]`, `['flag', name, value]`,\n`['quest', id, state]`, `['special', id]` (a hidden deed), `['secret', id]`, `['sfx', name]`, `['music', id]`,\n`['shake', n]`, `['return']` (an alcove gives its item back), `['take']` (an alcove keeps it), `['candlesOut']`,\n`['clock', id]`, `['checkpoint', id]` (the Rat Run), `['join', npc]`, `['npcGive', npc, itemId]`, `['npcLeave', npc]`.\n\n## Text and talk (`src/14-data-text.js`)\n\n`B.TXT` holds every string (messages, examine lines, inscriptions in capitals, notes, hints with `[act:name]` badges that\nbecome the player's own buttons). `B.STORY` holds conversations: steps `[who, text]`, `{ choices: [[label, node]] }`,\n`{ do: [actions] }`, `{ goto: node, if: 'full' | flag }`. `B.BARKS` are lines that do not stop play.\n\n## Items, monsters, spells, classes\n\n`src/10-data-items.js`, `11-data-monsters.js`, `12-data-spells.js`, `13-data-classes.js`: one entry each, plain data (see\neach file's header). An item's `icon` names a 12 x 12 pixel template in `61-ui-kit.js`; its `model` a pen model in\n`41-view-things.js`; a monster's look is in `42-view-creatures.js`.\n\n## The bot's steps (`walk`)\n\n`['go', x, y]`, `['use', x, y, face]`, `['take', x, y, item, face?]`, `['takeAll', area]`, `['clear', area]`,\n`['put' | 'throw' | 'place', x, y, face, item]`, `['equip', item, slot]`, `['choose', i]`, `['answerAll']`, `['wait', s]`,\n`['read', item]`, `['cast', spell, target]`, `['rest']`, `['restIfLow']`, `['scribeAll']`, `['fill', [features]]`,\n`['insert', x, y, face, item]`, `['unlatch', x, y, face]`, and the specials `buttons`, `gauntlet`, `candles`, `veil`,\n`reliquary`, `boss`.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Eye of the Bolt-Holder (dev folder)\n\nA real-time, first-person party dungeon crawler inspired by Eye of the Beholder (1991), built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the\n2D engine and its 3D engine over three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3), shipped as one HTML file in the folder above.\n\n## Build, test, play\n\n```sh\nnpm install                     # Playwright 1.63.0 (the browser tests and the AI Hub harness)\nnode tools/build.mjs            # writes ../EyeOfTheBoltHolder-...-20261103-185046.html and ../exit-interview.json\nnode tests/run.mjs              # every suite; prints only failures and one line\nnode tests/run.mjs --fast       # without the browser suites\nnode tests/run.mjs ui hub       # some suites\nnode tests/shoot.mjs [names]    # screenshots for review into shots/ (not a test)\n```\n\nOpen the root HTML from disk in a browser (three.js and Rapier load from jsDelivr). Deep links for testing:\n`#play` (a new game at once), `#warp/f2/10/2/1` (a floor and cell), `#race` (the Rat Run), `#attract`.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/` the game, concatenated in file order into one IIFE: `00-16` data, `20-31` the sim (pure, deterministic, no\n  page, sound or 3D), `40-44` the presenter (3D) and the Node stand-in, `50` audio, `60-68` input and UI, `70-73` Dev\n  Mode, attract, the bot and the AI Hub, `80` the cutscenes and stages, `90` the game and its scenes.\n- `engine/` the two engines, patched (`PATCHES.md`). `hub/` the AI Hub client and harness, unmodified.\n- `tests/` the runner, its suites, the Node loader, the browser helpers. `CONTENT.md` the data formats.\n\n## Controls\n\nPad (PlayStation layout): left stick step and strafe, d-pad step and turn, right stick flick turns, ✕ use (hold: put the\nHand down), ○ throw, □ Party Strike, L1 R1 choose a member, R2 L2 that member's hands, △ Party, L3 Camp, R3 Examine,\nCreate Map, Options pause. Keyboard: W S step, A D strafe, Q E turn (arrows step and turn), F use, H put down, G throw,\nSpace strike, Tab next member, 1-6 a member's main hand (Shift: off hand), I party, C camp, X examine, M map, J journal,\nEsc pause. Mouse: click things in the view, click hand slots to use them, right click to strike, drag items in the Party\nscreen.\nEOF\nls; cat tests/out/harness.log 2>/dev/null | tail -5","description":"Write PATCHES.md, CONTENT.md and README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3709,"cache_read_input_tokens":838161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3709},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"