e, a scene's data can be null (a default parameter did not catch it), a tap released before the next step reads as pressed but not down, and the 3D worlds run at about 3 frames a second under software rendering, so browser tests had to wait on game state rather than the clock.\",\n \"The crawler itself as a pure, deterministic sim: the grid party with tweened steps, the formation and per-hand combat, telegraphed monster minds, Vancian magic, camp and food, and a data-driven wiring language for doors, plates, levers, alcoves, teleporters and pits, plus the walkthrough bot that plays it all through the same commands as the player.\",\n \"Mixing its two UIs and testing the 3D: the engine's pause, settings and save screens are HTML while the game's 10-foot screens are drawn on the canvas, and every check of the 3D look had to run on SwiftShader, slowly.\",\n \"Two engines, small patches: in the 2D engine, beards and shut eyes for E.Humanoid, PlayStation and Xbox as the only button symbols (PlayStation first), a voice bus with its own volume, panned sound effects, Options ignored while Create is held (the AI Hub rule) and a way to hide Load in a session; in the 3D engine, world.wallBlock, a block made from the level's own wall materials so secret and illusory walls match the walls round them (PATCHES.md lists each).\",\n \"Let a 3D level's cells change at run time (a wall that opens, a floor that becomes a pit) instead of baking the level once, so secret walls, trapdoors and bridges would not need blocks laid over the baked geometry.\"\n]\npf = [\n \"It is complete and testable: exact deliverables, a detailed plan to build from, clear rules for tests (one command, failures only) and processes, and an exit interview in a fixed shape that the game's About screen can share.\",\n \"The title rule (brainstorm and pick by a random number) next to a plan that already fixed the title; and whether Online meant the game had to be multiplayer for a genre that is single-player at heart (the plan answered it with a ghost race).\",\n \"Fitting every system the plan lists (four floors, 16 monster types, 18 spells, camp, NPCs, three input styles, attract mode, Dev Mode, the hub race) into one build and still verifying the 3D look under software rendering.\",\n \"Say how long a first play of the demo should be and which systems may be cut if time runs short, and allow GPU rendering (or say it is unavailable) for screenshot checks.\"\n]\nimport json\ns=s.replace(\"  testingFeedback: ['', '', '', ''],\", \"  testingFeedback: \" + json.dumps(tf, ensure_ascii=False) + \",\")\ns=s.replace(\"  engineFeedback: ['', '', '', '', '', ''],\", \"  engineFeedback: \" + json.dumps(ef, ensure_ascii=False) + \",\")\ns=s.replace(\"  promptFeedback: ['', '', '', ''],\", \"  promptFeedback: \" + json.dumps(pf, ensure_ascii=False) + \",\")\ns=s.replace(\"    testing: 'Headless Node tests of the sim and UI through game.advance and game.debug (one command, tests/run.mjs, printing only failures and a count), a scripted full playthrough by the walkthrough bot on Normal with both of Veil\\\\'s branches, Playwright browser checks from file:// on SwiftShader, the AI Hub harness for 2 and 4 players with latency and loss and the host-leave case, and screenshots for the look',\",\n \"    testing: 'Any headless testing was allowed. Ran: 19 suites behind one command (tests/run.mjs, printing only failures and a count): lint and reachability of all content, movement, features, items, combat, monsters, magic, camp, progress, save, determinism, babble, UI flows, Dev Mode, attract mode and an AI Hub stub in Node through game.advance and game.debug; a scripted full playthrough by the walkthrough bot on Normal with both of Veil\\\\'s branches (also run over 20 seeds); Playwright browser checks from file:// on SwiftShader; the AI Hub harness for 2 players, 4 players with latency, jitter and loss, and the host leaving; screenshots at 1280x720 and 1024x768 for the look',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"testingFeedback: \\[\\\"About\" src/16-data-about.js; grep -c \"Any headless testing\" src/16-data-about.js; rm -rf tests/tmp; node tools/build.mjs","description":"Fill in the feedback answers and rebuild","timeout":200000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_017Do6z7eLaCdA3zGBQTuD5M":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-185046__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-185046"}}}
