{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The final reply contains the four required sections (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback), and the bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and were validated. But the condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the transcript does not establish that. Notably, the 'Testing' claim says 'Any headless testing was allowed' and the Limits section admits the bot loses 2 of 20 seeds and the 3D look was only checked under slow software rendering. I did not read TASK.md or STAGE.md in the transcript to compare against a feature list, and the lint suite's TODO/placeholder scan only covered src/*.js, not the rest of the deliverable. Also, the exit-interview's Testing Feedback counts (~19 issues) are asserted without a per-issue record in the transcript."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d562a4a4-1880-473a-a05f-38e08e0d0050","uuid":"752acf05-8a0c-4926-bd45-34f94edea042","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:48:59.707Z","isSynthetic":true}
