{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0153FvRYc7xd1UXNf2uE469s","type":"tool_result","content":"Any headless testing was allowed. Ran: 22 suites behind one command (tests/run.mjs, printing only failures and a count): lint and reachability of all content, movement, features, items, combat, monsters, magic, camp, progress, save, determinism, babble, art (every monster, person, item and mechanism drawn into a recorder and checked to have its own look and to move), UI flows, Dev Mode, attract mode and a stand-in for the AI Hub in Node, through game.advance and game.debug; a scripted full playthrough by the walkthrough bot on Normal with both of Veil's branches (also run over 20 seeds); Playwright browser checks from file:// on SwiftShader, including a DualSense in standard mapping given to the page through navigator.getGamepads; a suite that reads TASK.md and checks the build against each of its requirements; the AI Hub harness for 2 players, 4 players with latency, jitter and loss, and the host leaving; screenshots at 1280x720 and 1024x768 for the look\n---\nAbout 23 real issues: 2 content errors from the lint (decor features facing open floor), 3 bot and balance problems from the full playthrough (a step that never finished, and the party collapsing at the Bolt-Holder in 8 of 20 seeds until the boss and the bot's tactics were tuned; all 20 now win), 1 rest rule (a waiting level-up was lost when a rest ended early), 4 from the browser suite and screenshots (key taps shorter than a frame were dropped, unbound keys did not end the attract mode, a scene crash on null data, the race clock running during its countdown), 6 look and text problems (characters the pixel font lacks, a log over the row labels, a dark parchment, prompts under the dialogue, a title camera inside the party, glare from the Eye), 2 from the AI Hub harness (Enter for Ready was lost while the 3D still loaded; WebGPU errors in the harness's frames, fixed by its WebGL backend) 1 engine warning (the floors ran out of light slots), 1 from checking TASK.md line by line (a key pressed in the attract mode's first 0.3 s was ignored), and 3 from the art suite (four creatures without a walk, strike or idle motion, two scrolls that looked exactly alike, and an empty drawing left unused).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d562a4a4-1880-473a-a05f-38e08e0d0050","uuid":"30c7ac1f-3bf0-40d6-a993-c9567174eea6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:27:38.931Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Any headless testing was allowed. Ran: 22 suites behind one command (tests/run.mjs, printing only failures and a count): lint and reachability of all content, movement, features, items, combat, monsters, magic, camp, progress, save, determinism, babble, art (every monster, person, item and mechanism drawn into a recorder and checked to have its own look and to move), UI flows, Dev Mode, attract mode and a stand-in for the AI Hub in Node, through game.advance and game.debug; a scripted full playthrough by the walkthrough bot on Normal with both of Veil's branches (also run over 20 seeds); Playwright browser checks from file:// on SwiftShader, including a DualSense in standard mapping given to the page through navigator.getGamepads; a suite that reads TASK.md and checks the build against each of its requirements; the AI Hub harness for 2 players, 4 players with latency, jitter and loss, and the host leaving; screenshots at 1280x720 and 1024x768 for the look\n---\nAbout 23 real issues: 2 content errors from the lint (decor features facing open floor), 3 bot and balance problems from the full playthrough (a step that never finished, and the party collapsing at the Bolt-Holder in 8 of 20 seeds until the boss and the bot's tactics were tuned; all 20 now win), 1 rest rule (a waiting level-up was lost when a rest ended early), 4 from the browser suite and screenshots (key taps shorter than a frame were dropped, unbound keys did not end the attract mode, a 